# How to cite OpenDFX for Printed Circuit Boards (M11).
# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button.
# The same citations, in plain words, are on https://opendfx.org/cite/
# Add the DOI here once it is registered (M15).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book or its recommendations, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenDFX for Printed Circuit Boards"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Denney
    given-names: Chris
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: "https://opendfx.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OpenDFX/OpenDFX"
abstract: >-
  An open book of practical design-for-manufacturing, assembly and test
  recommendations for printed circuit boards. Each recommendation has a
  permanent ID, such as PCB-DFA-006, and a permanent address, such as
  https://opendfx.org/PCB-DFA-006. The text and drawings are licensed
  CC BY-SA 4.0. The recommendations data files are licensed CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - printed circuit board
  - PCB
  - design for manufacturing
  - design for assembly
  - design for test
  - DFM
  - DFA
  - DFT
  - electronics manufacturing
preferred-citation:
  type: book
  title: "OpenDFX for Printed Circuit Boards"
  authors:
    - family-names: Denney
      given-names: Chris
  year: 2026
  edition: "Version 1.0"
  url: "https://opendfx.org"
  license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
